TASK-201 runtime harness: a rule with included and excluded domains
(`lvh.me,~sub.lvh.me##.t201-ad`, `/t201-ad.js$domain=lvh.me|~sub.lvh.me`)
compiled in the running app hides and blocks on the included domain and not
on the excluded subdomain; every real list compiles with no rule stripped.
Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. Gated on DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR.

    SP=<scratch>; mkdir -p $SP/www $SP/out $SP/served
    # www/page.html: <script>window.__adRan = false</script>
    #                <script src="/t201-ad.js"></script>
    #                <div class="t201-ad"></div><div class="detour-control"></div>
    # www/t201-ad.js: window.__adRan = true;
    # served/<id>.txt: the four filter list texts (copies of the cached
    # lists, 2026-10-26); served/easylist.txt has the two rules above
    # appended. The harness's URLProtocol serves the list URLs from there
    # (no network).
    python3 -I -m http.server 8937 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory $SP/www &
    git apply docs/harness/task201-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    # run.sh (TASK-213's, adapted): waits for 12 s of HID idle, launches
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify2011 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR=$SP/out DETOUR_VERIFY_RUN=run2 \
        DETOUR_VERIFY_PORT=8937 DETOUR_VERIFY_LISTS=$SP/served \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # serves SHOOT lines with screencapture -l, kills only that PID after "done"
    git apply -R docs/harness/task201-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

lvh.me and all its subdomains resolve to 127.0.0.1 in public DNS, so one
loopback server answers for the included (lvh.me, www.lvh.me) and the
excluded (sub.lvh.me, x.sub.lvh.me) hosts. A fresh data directory fetches
all four lists (from the URLProtocol), parses and compiles them; the harness
waits until every list records rulesFormat 3, logs each list's "In List"
and "Active" counts, then opens the page on each host in turn and logs
window.__adRan, the computed display of .t201-ad and .detour-control, and
the tab's blockedCount.

Results (2026-10-27, the build with the fix, run2 on a fresh data dir):
    LIST easylist: rulesFormat=3 inList=71318 active=71318
    LIST easyprivacy: rulesFormat=3 inList=56310 active=56310
    LIST easylist-cookie: rulesFormat=3 inList=25079 active=25079
    LIST urlhaus-filter: rulesFormat=3 inList=102775 active=102775
    RESULT lvh.me: {"adScriptRan":false,"ad":"none","control":"block"} blockedCount=1
    RESULT www.lvh.me: {"adScriptRan":false,"ad":"none","control":"block"} blockedCount=1
    RESULT sub.lvh.me: {"adScriptRan":true,"ad":"block","control":"block"} blockedCount=0
    RESULT x.sub.lvh.me: {"adScriptRan":true,"ad":"block","control":"block"} blockedCount=0
The screenshots showed the same (the ad box gone on lvh.me and www.lvh.me,
shown on sub.lvh.me). run1 (data dir DetourVerify2010, logging before the
other lists had compiled) gave the same four RESULT lines. Before the fix
easylist-cookie compiled 25,077 of 25,079 (the two IDN rules stripped);
that was measured with a standalone parser + WKContentRuleListStore
bisection tool, not with this harness.

